{title: Greensleeves}
{artist: Traditional English}
{key: Am}
{rhythm: Slow Rock}
{license: public_domain}
{rights_holder: Public Domain}
{source: Traditional English Folk Song, 16th Century (London Stationers Register, 1580)}

A[Am]las, my [C]love, you [G]do me [Em]wrong
To [Am]cast me off dis[E]courteously
For [Am]I have [C]loved you [G]well and [Em]long
De[Am]lighting in [E]your com[Am]pany

[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my joy
[Am]Greensleeves was [E]my delight
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of gold
And [Am]who but my [E]lady [Am]Greensleeves

Thy [Am]music [C]still to [G]play and [Em]sing
When[Am]ever thou de[E]siredst it
And [Am]yet thou [C]wouldst not [G]love me [Em]back
Nor [Am]hearken [E]unto [Am]me

